# File:     packages/svelte-check/src/incremental.ts, emitSvelteFiles()
# Reason:   `svelte-check --tsgo` without `--incremental` starts from an empty
#           manifest, so pruneDeletedManifestEntries() never runs, yet emitDir
#           is never cleared. Every file in emitDir is part of the overlay
#           tsconfig program, so the svelte2tsx output of a DELETED .svelte
#           file keeps being type-checked and reports phantom errors. The same
#           happens in --incremental mode when the manifest is missing,
#           corrupt or of an old version. Fix: when there are no manifest
#           entries to prune from, start from an empty emitDir.
# Found by the U4 xoxd.ai lane, 2026-10-08. Applied to the bundle by
# patches/svelte-check@4.7.6.patch. Not filed upstream (operator channel only).
